# requirements/relativity/einstein-1919.ears
capability: Einstein 1919 examination
owner: relativity
requirements:
  - id: REL-001
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "Every transcribed measurement shall carry an uncertainty convention and a page or table locator."
    rationale: "Transcription errors and convention confusion are the main integrity risks of UC-02."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    gates: [REL-G-01]
    status: draft
    traces: []
  - id: REL-002
    pattern: unwanted
    text: "If a probable error enters a least-squares weight without explicit conversion, then the domain shall raise."
    rationale: "Probable errors quoted in 1920 overstate significance if used as standard errors."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: draft
    traces: []
  - id: REL-003
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "Deflection models shall take physical constants from a recorded CODATA version."
    rationale: "The module never hard-codes 1.75 arcsec."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    status: draft
    traces: []
  - id: REL-004
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The module shall fit each instrument set separately, and pooling shall require a PoolingJustification."
    rationale: "The instruments disagree; pooling hides that."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T1]
    gates: [REL-G-05]
    status: draft
    traces: []
  - id: REL-005
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The module shall evaluate all four hypotheses per instrument and per scenario."
    rationale: "Competing hypotheses are compared on equal footing."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T8]
    status: draft
    traces: []
  - id: REL-006
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The sensitivity sweep shall cover the six predeclared scenario axes."
    rationale: "Conclusions must survive every predeclared reduction choice."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T8]
    gates: [REL-G-06]
    status: draft
    traces: []
  - id: REL-007
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The fitter shall exist in two independent implementations that agree within tolerance."
    rationale: "Anything that issues a verdict is implemented twice."
    verification: test
    tiers: [T8]
    gates: [REL-G-08]
    status: draft
    traces: []
  - id: REL-008
    pattern: ubiquitous
    text: "The dossier shall list unrecoverable inputs and shall not describe a table-based reanalysis as a plate remeasurement."
    rationale: "A table-based reanalysis is not a plate remeasurement."
    verification: test
    tiers: []
    gates: [REL-G-09]
    status: draft
    traces: []
